  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return [[0]*9 for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find bounding box of non-zero elements\n    min_r, max_r = rows, -1\n    min_c, max_c = cols, -1\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                min_r = min(min_r, r)\n                max_r = max(max_r, r)\n                min_c = min(min_c, c)\n                max_c = max(max_c, c)\n    \n    # If no non-zero elements, return empty 9x9\n    if max_r == -1:\n        return [[0]*9 for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    height = max_r - min_r + 1\n    width = max_c - min_c + 1\n    \n    # Calculate cell dimensions for the 3x3 coarse grid\n    ch = height // 3\n    cw = width // 3\n    \n    # Ensure at least size 1 to avoid issues\n    if ch == 0:\n        ch = 1\n    if cw == 0:\n        cw = 1\n    \n    # Build the 3x3 binary mask M\n    M = [[0 for _ in range(3)] for _ in range(3)]\n    \n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            r_start = min_r + i * ch\n            r_end = min_r + (i + 1) * ch\n            c_start = min_c + j * cw\n            c_end = min_c + (j + 1) * cw\n            \n            # Check if this region contains any non-zero value\n            has_value = False\n            for r in range(r_start, min(r_end, rows)):\n                for c in range(c_start, min(c_end, cols)):\n                    if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                        has_value = True\n                        break\n                if has_value:\n                    break\n            M[i][j] = 1 if has_value else 0\n    \n    # Construct 9x9 output grid\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(9)] for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    # Fill output: for each cell in M, if it's 1, stamp the pattern M\n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            if M[i][j] == 1:\n                for di in range(3):\n                    for dj in range(3):\n                        if M[di][dj] == 1:\n                            output[3*i + di][3*j + dj] = 5\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return [[0]*9 for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Find bounding box of non-zero elements\n    min_r, max_r = rows, -1\n    min_c, max_c = cols, -1\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                min_r = min(min_r, r)\n                max_r = max(max_r, r)\n                min_c = min(min_c, c)\n                max_c = max(max_c, c)\n    \n    # If no non-zero elements, return empty 9x9\n    if max_r == -1:\n        return [[0]*9 for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    height = max_r - min_r + 1\n    width = max_c - min_c + 1\n    \n    # Calculate cell dimensions for the 3x3 coarse grid\n    ch = height // 3\n    cw = width // 3\n    \n    # Ensure at least size 1 to avoid issues\n    if ch == 0:\n        ch = 1\n    if cw == 0:\n        cw = 1\n    \n    # Build the 3x3 binary mask M\n    M = [[0 for _ in range(3)] for _ in range(3)]\n    \n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            r_start = min_r + i * ch\n            r_end = min_r + (i + 1) * ch\n            c_start = min_c + j * cw\n            c_end = min_c + (j + 1) * cw\n            \n            # Check if this region contains any non-zero value\n            has_value = False\n            for r in range(r_start, min(r_end, rows)):\n                for c in range(c_start, min(c_end, cols)):\n                    if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                        has_value = True\n                        break\n                if has_value:\n                    break\n            M[i][j] = 1 if has_value else 0\n    \n    # Construct 9x9 output grid\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(9)] for _ in range(9)]\n    \n    # Fill output: for each cell in M, if it's 1, stamp the pattern M\n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            if M[i][j] == 1:\n                for di in range(3):\n                    for dj in range(3):\n                        if M[di][dj] == 1:\n                            output[3*i + di][3*j + dj] = 5\n    \n    return output",
